        "title": "Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Remember that if <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a]</span> is a positive real number, then the derivative of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a^x]</span> is given by\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm d x}\\left( a^ x\\right)\t=\ta^ x \\ln a.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Remember that if [MATH: a] is a positive real number, then the derivative of [MATH: a^x] is given by\n[MATH: \\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm d x}\\left( a^ x\\right)\t=\ta^ x \\ln a.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>So, by &quot;reversing&quot; this process, we obtain the following formula for the integral of a general exponential function:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int  a^x \\, \\textrm d x  = \\dfrac{a^ x }{\\ln a} +C.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "So, by \"reversing\" this process, we obtain the following formula for the integral of a general exponential function:\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int a^x \\, \\textrm d x = \\dfrac{a^ x }{\\ln a} +C.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For instance, suppose that we wish to calculate the integral </p>",
            "readable_text": "For instance, suppose that we wish to calculate the integral",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\int 2^x  \\, \\textrm d x]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\int 2^x \\, \\textrm d x]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\int 2^x  \\, \\textrm d x   &amp;= \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln 2} + C\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\int 2^x \\, \\textrm d x &= \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln 2} + C\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nRemember that if [MATH: a] is a positive real number, then the derivative of [MATH: a^x] is given by\n[MATH: \\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm d x}\\left( a^ x\\right)\t=\ta^ x \\ln a.]\n\nContent:\nSo, by \"reversing\" this process, we obtain the following formula for the integral of a general exponential function:\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int a^x \\, \\textrm d x = \\dfrac{a^ x }{\\ln a} +C.]\n\nContent:\nFor instance, suppose that we wish to calculate the integral\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\int 2^x \\, \\textrm d x]\n\nContent:\nTo compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\int 2^x \\, \\textrm d x &= \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln 2} + C\n}]"
      },
