    ],
    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nRemember that the exponential function [MATH: e^x] has the special property that the derivative of the exponential function is the exponential function itself. In other words, taking the derivative doesn't change anything, and we have\n[MATH: \\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm d x} \\left(e^ x\\right) = e^ x.]\n\nContent:\nSince integration is the opposite of differentiation, and differentiating the exponential function leaves it unchanged, integrating the exponential function also leaves it unchanged. So, the integral of the exponential function is\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm d x = e^x +C.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Integrating the Exponential Function\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int 6e^x \\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFactoring out the constant [MATH: 6] and taking the integral, we get\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\int 6e^x \\textrm d x =6 \\int e^x \\, \\textrm d x =6e^x +C.\n\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b3e^{x}dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (3)/(e^{x}) + C]\nb. [MATH: 3e^{\\ln x} + C]\nc. [MATH: e^{3x} + C]\nd. [MATH: 3e^{x} + C]\ne. [MATH: (e^{x})/(3) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b \u2212 2e^{x}dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 2e^{x} + C]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 (2)/(e^{x}) + C]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 2e^{\\ln x} + C]\nd. [MATH: e^{\u2212 2x} + C]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 (e^{x})/(2) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base\n\nContent:\nRemember that if [MATH: a] is a positive real number, then the derivative of [MATH: a^x] is given by\n[MATH: \\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm d x}\\left( a^ x\\right)\t=\ta^ x \\ln a.]\n\nContent:\nSo, by \"reversing\" this process, we obtain the following formula for the integral of a general exponential function:\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int a^x \\, \\textrm d x = \\dfrac{a^ x }{\\ln a} +C.]\n\nContent:\nFor instance, suppose that we wish to calculate the integral\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\int 2^x \\, \\textrm d x]\n\nContent:\nTo compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\int 2^x \\, \\textrm d x &= \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln 2} + C\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int -6(7^x) \\, \\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we factor out the constant [MATH: -6.] Then, we integrate the exponential function, and get\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\int (-6)7^x \\, \\textrm d x\n&= -6\\int 7^x\\,\\textrm{d}x\\\n&=-6 \\cdot \\dfrac{7^x}{\\ln 7} + C.\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b4 \u22c5 5^{x}dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 4 \u22c5 (5^{\\ln x})/(\\ln 5) + C]\nb. [MATH: (\\ln x)/(\\ln 5) + C]\nc. [MATH: 2 \u22c5 (4^{x})/(\\ln 5) + C]\nd. [MATH: 4 \u22c5 (5^{x})/(\\ln 5) + C]\ne. [MATH: (5)/(\\ln x) + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \u222b3^{x}dx.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \\ln (3^{x}) + C]\nb. [MATH: 3^{x} + C]\nc. [MATH: (3^{x})/(\\ln 3) + C]\nd. [MATH: (\\ln x)/(\\ln 3) + C]\ne. [MATH: 3^{x}\\ln 3 + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Integrating a Sum of Exponential Functions\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x \\, \\textrm d x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nHere, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x \\, \\textrm d x &= \\displaystyle 5\\int 9^x \\, \\textrm{d}x+ 3 \\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n&= 5\\cdot \\dfrac{9^x}{\\ln 9} + 3 e^x +C.\n}]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b(2e^{x} + 4^{x} \u2212 2x)dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 2e^{x} + (4^{x})/(\\ln 4) \u2212 x^{2} + C]\nb. [MATH: e^{2x} + (4^{x})/(\\ln 4) \u2212 x^{2} + C]\nc. [MATH: 2e^{x} + 4^{x}\\ln 4 \u2212 (x^{2})/(2) + C]\nd. [MATH: e^{2x} + (x^{4})/(\\ln 4) \u2212 2x^{2} + C]\ne. [MATH: e^{2x} + (x^{4})/(\\ln 4) \u2212 x^{2} + C]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u222b(2^{x} \u2212 10e^{x})dx =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (x)/(\\ln 2) + e^{10x} + C]\nb. [MATH: (2^{x})/(\\ln|x|) \u2212 10e^{x} + C]\nc. [MATH: (x \u2212 2)/(\\ln 2) \u2212 10e^{x} + C]\nd. [MATH: (x^{2})/(\\ln 2) \u2212 e^{x} + C]\ne. [MATH: (2^{x})/(\\ln 2) \u2212 10e^{x} + C]"
  }
